# PhoneShell - the app's frame on a phone: a big title that shrinks into the bar as you scroll (the header never
# jumps in height), back on the left and at most two actions, and a bottom bar of three fixed tabs (the chosen one
# on --selected with its dot; a count never changes the width). Respects the phone's safe area.
#   PhoneShell(tabs: @tabs, rows: @rows, onSelect: pickTab)
# tabs {label, icon, badge} · rows {tab, section, title, subtitle, value}: each tab's screen is its rows, grouped by section.
# Drawn inside the library phone (DeviceFrame's rule). shadcn-for-muten · Custom (kit/structure.js) · kit.css (.cx-ph-*).
part PhoneShell(tabs: list, rows: list, onSelect: action) {
  Custom PhoneShell inputs(tabs: $tabs, rows: $rows) on(select: $onSelect) class("cx-ph-host")
}
